{%- comment -%}
  SEO metadata backfill.

  Horizon's stock snippets/meta-tags.liquid only emits a meta description when the
  page's SEO description is filled in in the Shopify admin, and only emits an
  og:image when Liquid can resolve a `page_image` — which never happens on custom
  /pages/* templates. The practical result was that every marketing page on this
  site shipped with no meta description and no social share image.

  This snippet fills both gaps WITHOUT duplicating tags: each block is guarded so it
  only fires when the stock snippet did not already emit that tag. Anything set in
  the Shopify admin always wins.

  Rendered from layout/theme.liquid immediately after 'meta-tags'.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign fallback_desc = ''

  comment
    Descriptions are Utah-first to match the titles in kw-seo-title. The three-state
    footprint is not hidden — it keeps its own page (mid-ohio-valley) and stays whole
    in the JSON-LD areaServed. What changes is which market each page leads with, so
    the homepage stops splitting its local signal three ways.
  endcomment
  if request.page_type == 'index'
    assign fallback_desc = 'Permanent Christmas, holiday and architectural lighting for Salt Lake City and Utah County homes. App-controlled, 10-year warranty, free estimates.'
  elsif request.page_type == 'page'
    case template.suffix
      when 'lighting'
        assign fallback_desc = 'Permanent architectural and holiday lighting installed across Salt Lake City and Utah County. App-controlled, freeze-thaw rated, 10-year warranty.'
      when 'solar'
        assign fallback_desc = 'Solar attic fan installation and solar panel care across Utah. Pull trapped heat out of your attic and keep your system producing. Free estimates.'
      when 'estimate'
        assign fallback_desc = 'Price your permanent lighting or solar attic fan install in about a minute. Real Kilowash rates for Utah homes, no sales call required.'
      when 'testimonials'
        assign fallback_desc = 'Real Kilowash installs and reviews from Utah homeowners — permanent lighting, solar attic fan and Critter Guard projects across the Wasatch Front.'
      when 'about'
        assign fallback_desc = 'A licensed and insured Utah team installing permanent architectural lighting and solar attic protection, with our own crews on every roof.'
      when 'contact'
        assign fallback_desc = 'Call or text the Kilowash crew for a free estimate on permanent lighting or solar attic fans anywhere we work in Utah. Fast response.'
      when 'mid-ohio-valley'
        assign fallback_desc = 'Kilowash installs permanent architectural lighting and solar attic fans across Washington, Noble and Morgan County OH and Wood County WV.'
      when 'critter-guard'
        assign fallback_desc = 'Pigeon and bird proofing for solar panels. Critter Guard mesh keeps birds and pests out from under your array, installed across Utah by Kilowash.'
      when 'panel-cleaning'
        assign fallback_desc = 'Solar panel cleaning and system care across Utah. Keep your array producing at full output. Licensed, insured, free estimates from Kilowash.'
      when 'city'
        assign fallback_desc = 'Permanent architectural and holiday lighting installed in ' | append: page.title | append: ', Utah. App-controlled, 10-year warranty, free on-site estimates.'
      else
        assign fallback_desc = settings.kw_seo_description
    endcase
  endif

  if fallback_desc == blank
    assign fallback_desc = settings.kw_seo_description
  endif
-%}

{%- comment -%}Only fires when the admin SEO description is empty — no duplicates.{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if page_description == blank and fallback_desc != blank -%}
  <meta name="description" content="{{ fallback_desc | escape }}">
{%- endif -%}

{%- liquid
  assign share_image = null
  if page_image
    assign share_image = page_image
  elsif settings.kw_seo_share_image != blank
    assign share_image = settings.kw_seo_share_image
  elsif settings.logo != blank
    assign share_image = settings.logo
  endif
-%}

{%- if share_image -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    og:image is only backfilled when the stock snippet skipped it (no page_image).
    twitter:image is always emitted — meta-tags.liquid never emits one at all, so
    link previews on X/Slack/iMessage currently fall back to nothing.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- unless page_image -%}
    <meta property="og:image" content="{{ share_image | image_url: width: 1200 | prepend: 'https:' }}">
    <meta property="og:image:secure_url" content="{{ share_image | image_url: width: 1200 | prepend: 'https:' }}">
  {%- endunless -%}
  <meta name="twitter:image" content="{{ share_image | image_url: width: 1200 | prepend: 'https:' }}">
{%- endif -%}
